>> title: Char Siu
>> category: Stews & Braises
>> tags: pork, chinese, roast, marinade, oven
>> counters: Dim Sum Counter, Takeout Counter, Phở & Bánh Mì, The Bowl Shop
>> aka: cha siu, chashao, 叉燒, 叉烧, xá xíu, xa xiu, BBQ pork, roast pork, red pork, barbecue pork
>> pairs-with: egg-fried-rice
>> servings: 6
>> time: 9 hr
>> slack: narrow — the last ten minutes is sugar under a hot oven: it goes from lacquer to carbon inside a minute, and it stays there
>> step.2: marinate chilled 8 hr
>> step.3: roast 425°F (220°C) 30 min, to 160°F (71°C)
>> step.4: stir into a pourable glaze
>> step.5: glaze, blister 10 min, rest 10 min, slice

Whisk @light soy sauce{3%Tbs}, @dark soy sauce{1%Tbs}, @Shaoxing wine{3%Tbs}, @hoisin sauce{3%Tbs}, @fermented red bean curd{2%cubes}(nam yu, mashed with 1 Tbs of its brine), @sugar{1/3%cup}(70 g), @Chinese five-spice powder{1%tsp}, @garlic{4%cloves}(grated), @fresh ginger{1%Tbs}(grated), @white pepper{1/4%tsp} into a smooth marinade.

Marinate @pork shoulder{3%lb}(1.35 kg; cut with the grain into 2-in-thick strips) in @&(~1)marinade{} in the fridge, turning once, for ~marinate{8%hr}.

Roast @&(~1)marinated pork{} on a rack over a foil-lined #sheet pan{} holding @water{1%cup}(240 mL), in a 425°F (220°C) #oven{} for ~roast{30%min}, turning once, to 160°F (71°C) at the centre.

Stir @maltose{3%Tbs}(60 g) with @honey{2%Tbs} and @hot water{1%Tbs} until pourable.

Brush @&(~1)glaze{} onto @&(~2)roast pork{} and return it to the #oven{} until the edges blacken and the glaze sets, ~roast{10%min}, then ~rest{10%min} and slice across the grain.
